---
const pieces = [
  {
    name: 'Nodes',
    caption: 'The pieces',
    example: 'A task · A contact · A page',
    description:
      'Each record has an identity of its own. Link pieces together without copying them into a new silo.'
  },
  {
    name: 'Schemas',
    caption: 'The common fit',
    example: 'Title + status + project',
    description:
      'Shared definitions describe the fields and relations. Builders can add their own fields or make a new kind of piece.'
  },
  {
    name: 'Views',
    caption: 'What you make with them',
    example: 'A table · A board · Your tool',
    description:
      'Different interfaces can use the same records. A new way to work doesn’t have to mean starting your data over.'
  }
]
---

<div class="substrate">
  <ol class="pieces" aria-label="Three parts of the xNet substrate">
    {pieces.map((piece, index) => (
      <li>
        <div class="piece-label">
          <span>0{index + 1}</span>
          <span>{piece.caption}</span>
        </div>
        <h3>{piece.name}</h3>
        <p class="piece-example">{piece.example}</p>
        <p class="piece-description">{piece.description}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
  <details class="mechanics">
    <summary>Under the hood: local copies, signed changes, shared rules</summary>
    <div class="m-grid-3">
      <p>
        <strong>Local first.</strong> The workspace stores a copy on your device. You can work
        offline and sync changes when connected.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>A record of change.</strong> Structured edits are signed and hash-linked. Peers can
        verify who signed an edit and detect changes to it.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Built to merge.</strong> Yjs merges document edits. Structured fields use
        deterministic last-writer-wins rules. Sharing is governed by grants and permissions.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="m-text-link" href="/docs/concepts/data-model/">
      Explore the data model <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </details>
</div>

<style>
  .substrate {
    margin-top: 48px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 18px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .pieces {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .pieces li {
    padding: 30px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .pieces li + li {
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .pieces li + li::before {
    content: '+';
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    position: absolute;
    top: 76px;
    left: -14px;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 9px;
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--forest);
  }
  .piece-label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font:
      10px/1.5 ui-monospace,
      monospace;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .piece-label > span:first-child {
    color: var(--forest);
  }
  h3 {
    margin-top: 24px;
    font-size: 32px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }
  .piece-example {
    margin-block: 18px;
    padding-block: 12px;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font:
      11px/1.6 ui-monospace,
      monospace;
    color: var(--forest);
  }
  .piece-description,
  .mechanics p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .mechanics {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: 22px 30px;
    background: var(--wash);
  }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .mechanics :global(.m-grid-3) {
    margin-block: 24px;
    gap: 32px;
  }
  .mechanics strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .pieces {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .pieces li {
      padding: 26px;
    }
    .pieces li + li {
      border-left: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }
    .pieces li + li::before {
      left: auto;
      right: 26px;
      top: -14px;
    }
    .mechanics {
      padding: 22px 26px;
    }
  }
</style>
